From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:21:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: drop the touchscreen
 pad's bias

MT6797's pin data has no pull registers, so the pad state's bias-disable
returns -ENOTSUPP. Each probe logged "pin_config_group_set op failed for
group 85", and the failure dropped the whole pad state, leaving the driver
core to continue without it. Touch still worked, because requesting the
interrupt sets the pad's EINT mode itself.

Remove the property, which also matches the keyboard's interrupt pad. The
pad's bias stays as firmware left it, which is what the touchscreen ran on.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 72460a4..31ebb06 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -239,7 +239,6 @@
 	touchscreen_pins: touchscreen-pins {
 		pins-irq {
 			pinmux = <MT6797_GPIO85__FUNC_EINT8>;
-			bias-disable;
 		};
 	};
 };
